+  "description": "Full building: lists of faces, edges, openings. Internal units are millimeters (unrounded); display converts to imperial (ft-in, sq ft, pitch x/12). US construction terms. v1.2 adds Hover-proven elements: roof flashing/step-flashing edges, three-stage pitch (original/rounded/snapped), soffit depth, window group_id, patio_door/skylight, chimney attachment, user_provided reference. Calculated values (waste, united inches, squares, gutter runs) stay in the calculation layer, NOT here. v1.3: heights.per_elevation + datum_note (sloped sites); building.footprint = MAIN BODY only, building.footprint_overall = envelope incl. attached volumes; attachments carry position_mm, parent_face_id, attached, include_in_footprint and dormer style/pitch so they can be placed and modeled. v1.4: faces carry color (hex + confidence) so the 3D viewer can render realistic surfaces; attachments add pipe/vent types so penetration counts by type (pipe boots, roof vents) are quotable; new downspouts array stores count/length/position explicitly (gutter RUNS stay derived from eave edges, downspout drops do not); new condition_areas array captures visible damage (failing paint, rot, sheathing damage) with face link, area and severity. v1.5: faces.material extended with roof covering materials (shingle_asphalt, shingle_wood, metal, tile, slate, membrane) so the covering type per roof face is quotable ($/SQ benchmark, metal-vs-shingle takeoff, tear-off type) and the viewer can group roof facets by covering material instead of color only. Conditional validation: roof_face accepts covering materials only, wall/soffit/fascia accept wall substrates only (metal valid for both) - misclassified extractions fail validation instead of reaching the viewer. v1.6: openings carry parent_face_id (the WL-n/RF-n they sit on) so an opening can be attributed to one wall even when an attached volume shares an elevation with the main body; wall faces carry width_mm, height_mm (grade to eave, rectangular part) and gable_height_mm so the gross area is reconstructable (width x height + 0.5 x width x gable) and checkable in code.",
